      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The stronger modern legal position often leans toward viewing expansive executive privilege as a dangerous erosion of checks and balances. While the President requires confidentiality to function, unlimited privilege can impede Congress's oversight and judicial review of executive actions. Courts generally seek a careful balance, accepting privilege only where the need for secrecy is paramount and outweighs the public interest in disclosure.",
